    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39334" root="نثر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْتَثِرٌ</span></b>  <i>In a scattered</i> or <i>strewn state; in a state
of dispersion;</i> (M;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَنَاثِرٌ</span></b> , (TA,) and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَثَرٌ</span></b> , which last is applied to a thing and to
things. (M.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِثَارٌ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُثَارٌ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْثُورٌ</span>.
You say ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُرٌّ مُتَنَاثِرٌ</span></b>  [<i>Pearls in a scattered state</i>].
(TA.)

